    <statement><p>Let <m>\ y = 9 x^{6} - 3961 x^{2}  + 6 \ </m>.</p>
<p>(a) What power function does the function above resemble?
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/>  
(Enter the entire power function, not just the degree of the power function.)</p>
<p>(b) Describe the long-run behavior of the polynomial.
Enter <alert> INFINITY </alert> or  <alert> -INFINITY </alert>
for <m>\infty</m> or <m>- \infty</m>.</p>
<p><m>y</m> goes to <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0002"/> as <m>x \to \infty</m></p>
<p><m>y</m> goes to <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0003"/> as <m>x \to - \infty</m>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>9x^{6}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\infty </m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\infty </m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



Since the leading term of the polynomial is <m>9 x^{6}</m>,
the value of <m>y</m> goes to <m>\infty</m> as <m>x \to \infty</m> and
<m>\infty</m> as <m>x \to - \infty</m>.



</solution>
